  },
  {
    "file": "screen011.png",
    "sha256": "a5e7a6ecd09208afac59dc1ec738d4a5dd9a796f048f849a71bc6461e6af95cd",
    "k": 10,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "transition",
    "en": "Questions one to five are based on part one of the interview.",
    "zh": "第1至5题根据访谈的第一部分提问。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "be based on"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen012.png",
    "sha256": "13af85555cdf7c83ef512d02b13a0ea30fe08e211ac799d2877cb4f81a2699a9",
    "k": 11,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "The word diversity has become a cliché in the United States today.",
    "zh": "如今在美国，“多样性”这个词已成了老生常谈。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "cliché"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen013.png",
    "sha256": "94bc626161a3a70c977fd7d34705c7d1dbe059f0d12d5f5524bbf3339569c1fc",
    "k": 12,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "It seems to me that nowadays Americans cannot turn on the television or read a newspaper ",
    "zh": "在我看来，如今美国人只要打开电视或翻开报纸，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "turn on"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen014.png",
    "sha256": "184b6751c77d63a9760c627b925b1e0086cd8218427e6f68d7bc0cce2acccb63",
    "k": 12,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "without seeing the word pop up somewhere as a description of the American demographic.",
    "zh": "就会在某处看到这个词，用来描述美国的人口构成。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "pop up"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen015.png",
    "sha256": "b9b574c1460e855dd5145b16ef21298b7eebdc62b09b2420ce92cb746517b57e",
    "k": 13,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Then what is this diversity in the US?",
    "zh": "那么，美国所说的这种多样性到底是什么呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "diversity"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen016.png",
    "sha256": "36c522008fc158236476731fe0b3f1458e0ff58540169929e4e84e63222bb974",
    "k": 14,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Today, we are very pleased to have Dr James Johnson here on our talk show.",
    "zh": "今天，我们很高兴邀请到詹姆斯·约翰逊博士做客访谈节目。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "talk show"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen017.png",
    "sha256": "8a51d645db570496fe6364c4811449d6e2185de55a1e7ac877548de499369195",
    "k": 15,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Welcome, Dr Johnson.",
    "zh": "欢迎您，约翰逊博士。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "welcome"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen018.png",
    "sha256": "532b5fa2ea4f2d45e80b31c00b45bc6d40192e536b06470a40d4ea36f18642e3",
    "k": 16,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Thanks.",
    "zh": "谢谢。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Thanks"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen019.png",
    "sha256": "c42ca6667f7dd9822e691cd2dd956ac9964c427d9084ec3356704f525e7231a5",
    "k": 17,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Dr Johnson, we know you have done extensive research on diversity.",
    "zh": "约翰逊博士，我们知道，您对多样性做过广泛的研究。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "extensive"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen020.png",
    "sha256": "e9e93fe04de60d06ac3f4b99302c21a018bcd960749aabddb421e06fdadd7c3b",
    "k": 18,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So, what is, how do you define diversity in the American context?",
    "zh": "那么，什么是……您如何定义美国社会语境中的多样性？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "context"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen021.png",
    "sha256": "8f2aa6f69064a57730351abbb5f232e638800d584554f8f6d25ebfbf8a57216e",
    "k": 19,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Well, at one time the US was called a melting pot, you know, which means that people of many different religions, cultures, and races ",
    "zh": "嗯，美国曾被称为“大熔炉”，也就是说，信仰、文化和种族各不相同的人，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "melting pot"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen022.png",
    "sha256": "3d30df0276953e83c55efd3c15ff2dfe25741f537596123bcfb249d95e3efc6d",
    "k": 19,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "could shed their traditional cultural identities and blend into one homogeneous nation.",
    "zh": "可以放下原有的传统文化身份，融合为一个同质的国家。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "shed"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen023.png",
    "sha256": "bb72ed6bc9ccf1a8c429694139bc6921c8fc31bf1f036db22c4f3561be8a3683",
    "k": 20,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Am I right in saying that a melting pot would emphasize the idea of all in one or being the same?",
    "zh": "我可以这样理解吗：大熔炉强调的是融为一体，或者变得相同？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "emphasize"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen024.png",
    "sha256": "5489b97a24efdae7e2fa1ff26295f4847d4e7f011a4dda7ee0de5e4cf6c25da5",
    "k": 21,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Yes, you may say so.",
    "zh": "是的，可以这么说。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "may say so"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen025.png",
    "sha256": "9f318274d1d823e020cd962b9f9235a3320eb064524fd5329b79401ff30a779a",
    "k": 22,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Um, of course, when the phrase “melting pot” was popular, there was also the idea of being different, ",
    "zh": "嗯，当然，在“大熔炉”这个说法流行时，也存在差异的观念，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "melting pot"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen026.png",
    "sha256": "0ac70ffee23287db1a837df9d06b934bbb17627ed5d8972736f855c3003537a6",
    "k": 22,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "but being different then simply meant Catholic as opposed to Protestant, or Irish as opposed to Swedish or Italian.",
    "zh": "不过那时所谓的不同，只是天主教徒相对于新教徒，或者爱尔兰裔相对于瑞典裔、意大利裔的差别。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "as opposed to"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen027.png",
    "sha256": "8bdb07a0da96847d1c8c28b368a2bbf26ba2984a98a7b86a1f2e99f251b9b033",
    "k": 23,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Has the idea of being different changed over the years?",
    "zh": "这些年来，人们对于“不同”的理解发生变化了吗？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "over the years"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen028.png",
    "sha256": "81621d918c0832566d99b65774fbee5abcd92166f5a38b97e843727902daecbf",
    "k": 24,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Yes, of course.",
    "zh": "是的，当然发生了变化。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "of course"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen029.png",
    "sha256": "80a6ba1a68ba0874d6da5bd34a57c2280dd32bd14394eb714d7751f45888db04",
    "k": 25,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "You see today, we use the word diversity to refer to more-visible ethnic differences — ",
    "zh": "你看，如今我们用“多样性”指更为明显的族裔差异，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "ethnic"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen030.png",
    "sha256": "3dba2bbbaf26f1288daadfdd6522ae396e5c15a341047a67a85c77a2f0e353f7",
    "k": 25,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Asian American, African American, and Latino, for instance.",
    "zh": "例如亚裔美国人、非裔美国人以及拉丁裔。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Latino"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen031.png",
    "sha256": "8363bb23a859fa1a33d0cda6910897344d525847356eede0c9109aca08b05640",
    "k": 26,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And religious diversity refers to a variety of world religions, not merely different branches of Christianity.",
    "zh": "宗教多样性指的是世界上的各种宗教，而不仅仅是基督教内部的不同教派。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "branch"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen032.png",
    "sha256": "832f4ee249159f0220337de0957e271ab0dc2096c25334baab72a0507cc45201",
    "k": 27,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And now is America as a whole truly diverse?",
    "zh": "那么，如今美国整体上真的具有多样性吗？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "as a whole"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen033.png",
    "sha256": "bc2b038ab1b9c3a2c82d87b8671ad93f79d87db874168e9219f4bbe43db4ad86",
    "k": 28,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Well, I think in all this talk of diversity there is a critical point that may be missed: that is, ",
    "zh": "嗯，我认为，在所有这些关于多样性的讨论中，人们可能忽略了一个关键点：",
    "vocabulary": [
      "critical point"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen034.png",
    "sha256": "77a13523d27a702f323ba96a2ecb275b1c59ff660d803767fccb2d19c811e6af",
    "k": 28,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "diversity is not occurring everywhere in the US, or at least not to a degree that would alter the demography of every region in the country.",
    "zh": "多样化并未发生在美国所有地方，至少还没有达到改变全国每个地区人口构成的程度。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "demography"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen035.png",
    "sha256": "5b3f24ecd4ba76b7d3e1a6c3f5ee181ea5d295f8faf11b47ebc2bd73285516f9",
    "k": 29,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Oh, really?",
    "zh": "哦，是这样吗？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "really"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen036.png",
    "sha256": "ffd0197dcae7ea69508870f54a2ab7426c40b898f3754007ad8c43b27766d0a2",
    "k": 30,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "I can give you an example.",
    "zh": "我可以举个例子。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "give an example"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen037.png",
    "sha256": "9fa4d9ae3458c326b1fde68402377c7a8176dccdd74b74fd0c206b84a5e01bee",
    "k": 31,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Recently a New York Times article describes the town of Selinsgrove in Pennsylvania.",
    "zh": "最近，《纽约时报》的一篇文章介绍了宾夕法尼亚州的塞林斯格罗夫镇。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "describe"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen038.png",
    "sha256": "08151c429c0801d5819ec4202d584ef1c5da10959762972ede8120ac1b0a781e",
    "k": 32,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "You see, in the last 10 years things have barely changed in that town.",
    "zh": "你看，过去十年里，那个小镇几乎没有变化。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "barely"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen039.png",
    "sha256": "39b8f4d8439e9acfc10cbaa6dfc5c79573fd5ff5ef1cd92a09057dc6fbea943c",
    "k": 33,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "The population has dropped by one, from 5,384 to 5,383 and the town remains virtually 100% white.",
    "zh": "人口只减少了一人，从5384人降到5383人，而镇上的居民仍然几乎百分之百是白人。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "virtually"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen040.png",
    "sha256": "cb5fbe2330997d8ba968ff1d0e5774bb7ccf09001e7e83aeb2e486b9f03fb69c",
    "k": 34,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "The article thus concludes that many portions of the country remain, like Selinsgrove, virtually unchanged on this march towards “diversity.”",
    "zh": "因此，这篇文章得出结论：在迈向“多样性”的进程中，美国的许多地方仍像塞林斯格罗夫一样，几乎没有变化。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "conclude"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen041.png",
    "sha256": "816cc0359a3d6ba4bf9123c5b589bbd56bcb64e8cdb79bce7cf1b47e9634fa84",
    "k": 35,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So regions vary in terms of the degree and types of diversity?",
    "zh": "所以，各地区多样性的程度和类型有所不同，是吗？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "in terms of"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen042.png",
    "sha256": "14f8a9f8f85742eeaa5d3f9aa5f9fa56a437d9df41d586d060c082571d77ac27",
    "k": 36,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "That’s correct.",
    "zh": "没错。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "correct"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen043.png",
    "sha256": "0e4a968c86e0653b26bb168bb838818e8104dab0264b90d751808436f4f37813",
    "k": 37,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Let’s say there are 3 types of diversity in the US.",
    "zh": "我们姑且说，美国存在三种多样性。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Let’s say"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen044.png",
    "sha256": "cc8df775e1f767956c687264f594e6782f13d360b5d914c355dc8c8353746610",
    "k": 38,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And they differ from region to region.",
    "zh": "而且，它们因地区而异。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "differ from region to region"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen045.png",
    "sha256": "f101c968d0308a8657a5a3369a2d2b3179745df486a7337ecb317b672a30d56e",
    "k": 39,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Could you elaborate on that?",
    "zh": "您能详细说明一下吗？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "elaborate on"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen046.png",
    "sha256": "e11cdf155a30b42bc0f366c1fe97c9c5e65119b5e227ad3439b6523b4012755a",
    "k": 40,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "OK. The first is racial diversity.",
    "zh": "好的。第一种是种族多样性。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "racial"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen047.png",
    "sha256": "4e406b2fb9e422fad6429b727e01e9b9f17dff7177875bae6051a1b9d35dc9ca",
    "k": 41,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "States with the most racially diverse populations stand in stark contrast to those with the least racially diverse populations.",
    "zh": "人口种族构成最多样的州，与种族构成最单一的州形成了鲜明对比。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "stand in stark contrast to"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen048.png",
    "sha256": "7cc8f734a3960179fde1b7d35e35129d1ca54c2327e1d043a8bf05ffe8a6be19",
    "k": 42,
